    contentHTML:
      '<div class="learn-intro">Animals reproduce sexually (most) or asexually (some). Sexual reproduction involves the fusion of male and female gametes. This topic covers types of reproduction, fertilisation, development, and parental care in animals.</div><h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Types of Reproduction</h3><ul class="learn-list"><li><strong>Asexual:</strong> binary fission (Amoeba, bacteria), budding (Hydra, yeast), fragmentation (Planaria), parthenogenesis (aphids, Daphnia)</li><li><strong>Sexual:</strong> requires gametes (sperm + egg); fertilisation restores diploid number</li></ul><h3 class="learn-subheading">2. External vs Internal Fertilisation</h3><div class="learn-table-wrap"><table class="learn-table"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>External</th><th>Internal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Location</td><td>Outside body (in water)</td><td>Inside female reproductive tract</td></tr><tr><td>Gametes produced</td><td>Very large numbers (wasteful)</td><td>Fewer gametes needed</td></tr><tr><td>Parental care</td><td>Usually minimal</td><td>Usually more extensive</td></tr><tr><td>Success rate</td><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td></tr><tr><td>Examples</td><td>Fish, frogs, most aquatic animals</td><td>Reptiles, birds, mammals</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Development</h3><ul class="learn-list"><li><strong>Oviparous:</strong> lay eggs (fish, amphibia, birds, reptiles, monotremes)</li><li><strong>Viviparous:</strong> give birth to live young; embryo nourished via placenta (most mammals)</li><li><strong>Ovoviviparous:</strong> eggs retained in mother but no placental connection (some sharks, snakes)</li></ul><h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Human Reproduction</h3><ul class="learn-list"><li>Male: testes produce sperm; testosterone secreted</li><li>Female: ovaries produce eggs; oestrogen and progesterone regulate menstrual cycle (~28 days)</li><li>Menstrual cycle: menstruation → follicular phase → ovulation (day 14) → luteal phase</li><li>Placenta: exchanges nutrients, gases, waste between mother and foetus</li><li>Gestation: ~9 months (40 weeks) in humans</li></ul><div class="learn-tip-box"><span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span><strong>Menstrual Cycle:</strong> FSH → follicle matures → oestrogen rises → LH surge → ovulation (day 14) → corpus luteum → progesterone → maintains uterine lining.</div><div class="learn-tip-box"><span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> External fertilisation (aquatic, many gametes). Internal fertilisation (terrestrial, fewer gametes, higher success). Oviparous (eggs). Viviparous (live birth, placenta). Menstrual cycle ~28 days; ovulation ~day 14.</div>',
